  "notes": [
    "WADAT_IST is the canonical example of why technical metadata is necessary: 'when did it ship' cannot be resolved to LIKP-WADAT_IST without this layer.",
    "Many SAP fields have generic names (BUDAT appears in AFRU, MKPF, MSEG with different business meanings). Context from the table name is essential.",
    "DATS fields are stored as YYYYMMDD character strings in SAP; the staging model casts them to proper DATE types.",
    "This extract is illustrative; a production semantic layer would include all fields from the relevant tables, versioned and refreshed quarterly as the data model evolves."
  ],
